---
import { Icon } from '@santi020k/lumen-astro'

import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro'
---

<Base
  title="Architecture"
  description="How the shared standards, read-only catalog, agent plugins, and documentation website fit together in a pnpm Turborepo."
>
  <header class="page-intro">
    <p class="eyebrow">Built to stay understandable</p>
    <h1>
      One source.
      <br />
      <em>Several ways in.</em>
    </h1>
    <p class="lead">
      Markdown holds the decisions. A typed catalog makes them discoverable.
      Each agent gets the integration it understands.
    </p>
  </header>
  <section
    class="architecture-flow"
    aria-label="How guidance reaches people and agents"
  >
    <div>
      <p class="tiny-label">01 / Source</p>
      <h2>Standards & decisions</h2>
      <p>Versioned Markdown, explicit scope, and source metadata.</p>
      <code>standards/ + docs/</code>
    </div>
    <Icon name="arrow-down" aria-hidden="true" />
    <div>
      <p class="tiny-label">02 / Shared package</p>
      <h2>Catalog, CLI & MCP</h2>
      <p>
        Search and retrieve locally. Preview configuration changes with a
        rollback path.
      </p>
      <code>@santi020k/way</code>
    </div>
    <Icon name="arrow-down" aria-hidden="true" />
    <div class="destinations">
      <div>
        <h3>Codex</h3>
        <p>Global guidance + plugin</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>Claude Code</h3>
        <p>Global guidance + plugin</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>The website</h3>
        <p>Readable, searchable references</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">Intentional boundaries</p>
      <h2>
        Every part
        <br />
        has an owner.
      </h2>
    </div>
    <div class="area-list">
      <a class="area-row" href="/standards/0001-shared-sources/">
        <span class="row-number">01</span>
        <div>
          <h3>Share sources; adapt delivery.</h3>
          <p>
            Why the catalog is local, the plugins are generated, and Lumen keeps
            its component contracts.
          </p>
        </div>
        <Icon name="arrow-up-right" aria-hidden="true" />
      </a>
      <a class="area-row" href="/standards/0002-local-configuration/">
        <span class="row-number">02</span>
        <div>
          <h3>Keep machine configuration local.</h3>
          <p>
            Why a guidance update preserves your settings, requires an exact
            preview, and keeps a recovery receipt.
          </p>
        </div>
        <Icon name="arrow-up-right" aria-hidden="true" />
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
